      palaceRoomConnections: ["BL", "SR", "GR"],
      practicalExercise:
        "Write a one-page summary of the three angels' messages as you would explain them to a sincere Christian friend from another denomination who has never encountered these truths. Use simple, warm language — avoid Adventist jargon. Include key Scripture references (KJV) and focus on the love and urgency behind each message. Share your summary with your study group for feedback on clarity and tone.",
      weeklyChallenge:
        "Identify one person in your life — perhaps a Bible study contact or a friend with spiritual interest — and prayerfully share one element of the three angels' messages with them this week. It could be as simple as sharing the significance of the Sabbath as a memorial of creation, or the hope of Christ's soon return. Pray before the conversation, trust the Holy Spirit during it, and journal about it afterward.",
